headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

auth {
  mode: oauth2
}

auth:oauth2 {
  grant_type: client_credentials
  access_token_url: http://localhost:8091/realms/het-security-realm/protocol/openid-connect/token
  refresh_token_url: 
  client_id: home-energy-tracker-client
  client_secret: {{process.env.HET_CLIENT_SECRET}}
  scope: 
  credentials_placement: body
  credentials_id: het-token
  token_source: access_token
  token_placement: header
  token_header_prefix: Bearer
  auto_fetch_token: true
  auto_refresh_token: true
}

docs {
  Token do Keycloak (realm het-security-realm, client home-energy-tracker-client,
  grant client_credentials) salvo com o id het-token.

  Para usar numa requisicao:
  - Auth > Inherit: herda esta configuracao e manda o Authorization sozinho;
  - ou, em qualquer outro lugar, {{$oauth2.het-token.access_token}}.

  O client secret vem de bruno/.env (HET_CLIENT_SECRET), que nao vai para o git -
  copie bruno/.env.example e preencha com o secret da aba Credentials do client.

  As requisicoes direto nos servicos continuam com Auth > No Auth, entao nada
  muda para elas.
}
